# WARNING: HEAVY SPOILERS #

LORE:
    Intro:
        - normal life story until strange things happen (POV: Mina, Planet of Truth)

        Planet of Truth:
            - ages ago, a group of scientists on the planet figured out how to arrange the common stone-like mineral on their planet into a transparent solid
            - they used it in windows, glassware, etc., but then these same scientists noticed:
            - when answering a question while in contact with the mineral, they were not able to think and speak the exact words they wanted to say
            - the mineral turned out to be a kind of truth "serum":
                - for: any contacting consciousness that is in control of a body that is physically in contact with the mineral
                - it causes: only being able to answer questions directed at them with true statements
                - with low amounts of the mineral, the influenced answers are restricted to yes/no and also restricted in complexity
                - the larger the amount of mineral connected to a question receiver, the more complicated the question can be and the more detailed the influenced answer is
                - BUT: subjective questions are not influenced
            - the people of the planet decided to put traces of the mineral into the water supply, so that no one could seriously lie again
            - side effect: with the mineral in your system, you can ask yourself a simple question and get a "magical" true answer without asking anyone else
            Max & Ben encounter:
                - Max appears, as people of the planet look up at him
                - Max (using nanobots to lift and protect him) floats through the clouds, ripping holes through them, then comes to a stop mid-air (he actually uses this maneuver as a way of quickly spreading his nanobots everywhere he can)
                - he speaks to the people that can see him in a calm voice, which they hear as if he was standing right in front of them (through nanobot speakers in their ears)
                    - offers to rule over the planet as an absolute ruler
                        - who will take the moon as a source of minerals and will put the people under constant surveillance
                        - declining will mean their planet will also be turned into ressources, along with the people
                    - disappears to be back the next day at the same time for an answer
                        - also caused by nano appearing to lecture him, hitting him into the ground and then into space (this is where the nano-max fight happens, nano "loses" and max returns the next day)
                - the eldest of all regions gather with all the mineral they can gather and ask it if and why they should accept
                    - the truth is revealed, that under the condition that protecting their people (goal: greatest happiness of the greatest number) is the most important thing for them, they must accept temporarily, because their opponent is truly that powerful
                    - they do have the ability to seek help
                        - and are recommended to visit a shrine on the top of a mountain, meeting someone who can free them (Ban as his female representation Bun) there
                - at the shrine, Bun requests a favor that will bring her joy
                - because her grandpa is one of the elders, he lets Mina accompany him to the shrine
                - lost in thoughts about what to do, she walks through the forest and finds an artifact
                    - inspects it, picks it up and asks: what makes you happy?
                    - the voice of Bun starts talking in her head: I find joy in doing the incredible and others seeing it. Just removing the intruders from your people, you could not see and witness that with your own eyes. You can't express joy at my heroic act, so I don't get any either. Find a way to let me show you what I am capable of, and if you're amazed, I'm happy. I know you won't lie about if you're impressed.
                    - the artifact makes you able to ask any question to someone from within your mind:
                        - the thoughts will spell out an answer just like the actual person would have said it
                        - doesn't cause the actual person to know they got asked something
                - Mina tells her grandpa what they should offer
                - ...
                - during Max' request for an answer, he suddenly changes his mind, decides on leaving the people of that planet autonomous, retreats all of his nanobots and continues on to the next system
                - they return to the shrine to thank Bun, but instead of the shrine there is now a lump of metal on the mountain
                - after the metal is mined, they discover that the whole mountain is now also made of various metals

        - transition to backstory of Ben / Ban & Max

    Max Lore:
        ☐ Max turns out to be a spy and Nanos right hand man
        ☐ but plans to overthrow Nano
        ☐ Max goes to find and enslave planets of other systems
        ☐ this upsets nano -> fight
        ☐ Max wins barely
        ☐ secretly, Nano sees all this coming and retreats, assuming Max will change if he wins
        ☐ Max doesn't change, but nano only finds out when he gets to the hivemind planet
        ☐ Nano returns and ends Max after max did the most terrible thing

    hivemind planet:
        - all living beings on this planet are found to be one giant hivemind, and everything works as one
        - created nano --with-consideration-for-nano-willingly-"losing"-in-the-fight-against-Max--> final boss planet for Max

    supernaturals:
        emotions girl:
            abilities:
                - feeling emotions of anything with enough physical contact (stronger emotions can already be felt through less, spreads like voltage [high potential spreads more easily])
                - moving emotions through physical contact and concentration (larger contact surface and more developed skill increases speed)
            scenarios:
                - meeting someone with remote aura for the first time (finds out she can feel emotions by just being close [handshake hasn't connected yet, pulls back unexpectedly], if they are stong enough)
                - meeting someone with immense aura of negative emotions (gets overwhelmed by just being within line of sight)
        ban (post nano Ben):
            - playing with peoples minds, feelings and reality
            - eventually finds someone of the same capabilities as him
            - turns out he met a clone he created in his sleep (he dreamt about having a friend who is on his level)
            - so they become friends immediately because the clone is a product of his imagination

